No problem — you just need to install **screen** first.

---

# ✅ Step 1 — Install screen

Run this:

```bash
sudo apt install screen
```

Enter your password if asked.

---

# ✅ Step 2 — Open Bluetooth Console

After installation, run:

```bash
screen /dev/rfcomm0 115200
```

You will now enter the Bluetooth console.

---

# ✅ Step 3 — Send commands to ESP32

Inside screen, type:

```
F
```

(press ENTER)

```
B
```

(ENTER)

```
S
```

(ENTER)

```
speed:200
```

(ENTER)

Your motors should respond immediately.

---

# 🛑 To exit screen

Press:

```
Ctrl + A
K
```

Then press **Y**.

